+# HITTER Ready Pose MuJoCo Isolated Test Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Add the user-selected bilateral ready pose to an isolated RobotBridge2 test worktree so the user can validate recovery-to-waiting behavior in MuJoCo without changing or starting the original `loco1` checkout.
+
+**Architecture:** Keep the saved YAML/JSON as audit artifacts, but inline the exact 14 named joint values in the isolated Hydra config because the current runtime has no pose-file loader. `HitterEnv` validates the configuration once, maps names to the exact simulation indices `15..28`, and applies a deterministic 0.9-second smoothstep only while the lifecycle is WAITING or TRACKING. ARMED and RECOVERY always receive the unmodified ONNX PD target.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Python 3.8, NumPy, OmegaConf/Hydra, `unittest`, RobotBridge2 MuJoCo runtime.
+
+## Global Constraints
+
